       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum labeled daily dose of 2550 mg for immediate-release metformin (2000 mg/day for extended-release). Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a high risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPlease confirm the intended regimen. Common options are:\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1500 mg/day)\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2550 mg/day, the labeled maximum for IR)\n- **1700 mg PO once daily with the evening meal**, if an extended-release product is intended (within the 2000 mg/day ER maximum)\n\nOr, if 1700 mg TID is really intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order."
